    "['vsi [name] [type]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances ldp1 instance-type l2vpn', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-instances ldp1 instance-type l2vpn', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-instances ldp1 instance-type l2vpn\\nset routing-instances ldp1 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\nset routing-instances ldp1 protocols l2vpn site 1 site-id 1 remote-site-id 2\\n##  \\n\\n(Note: In Juniper, the equivalent of a Huawei static VSI with LDP signaling would be an L2VPN routing instance with LDP signaling. The \"static\" nature is implied by the direct configuration of the site parameters rather than dynamic discovery. The peer IP mapping would be handled separately under MPLS/LDP configuration.)', 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances ldp1 instance-type l2vpn'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances ldp1 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-instances ldp1 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-instances ldp1 instance-type l2vpn\\nset routing-instances ldp1 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\nset routing-instances ldp1 protocols l2vpn site 1 site-id 1 remote-site-id 2\\n##  \\n\\n(Note: In Juniper, the equivalent of a Huawei static VSI with LDP signaling would be an L2VPN routing instance with LDP signaling. The \"static\" nature is implied by the direct configuration of the site parameters rather than dynamic discovery. The peer IP mapping would be handled separately under MPLS/LDP configuration.)', 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances ldp1 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-instances ldp1 protocols l2vpn site 1 site-id 1 remote-site-id 2', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set routing-instances ldp1 protocols l2vpn site 1 site-id 1 remote-site-id 2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset routing-instances ldp1 instance-type l2vpn\\nset routing-instances ldp1 interface GigabitEthernet1/0/1.1\\nset routing-instances ldp1 protocols l2vpn site 1 site-id 1 remote-site-id 2\\n##  \\n\\n(Note: In Juniper, the equivalent of a Huawei static VSI with LDP signaling would be an L2VPN routing instance with LDP signaling. The \"static\" nature is implied by the direct configuration of the site parameters rather than dynamic discovery. The peer IP mapping would be handled separately under MPLS/LDP configuration.)', 'trans_template': 'set routing-instances ldp1 protocols l2vpn site 1 site-id 1 remote-site-id 2'}]]": 1,
    "['pwsignal [protocol]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'protocols l2vpn', 'parent_command': ['set routing-instances ldp1 instance-type l2vpn'], 'root': 'set routing-instances ldp1 instance-type l2vpn', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nprotocols l2vpn\\n##\\n\\nThe `pwsignal ldp` command in Huawei's configuration specifies that LDP (Label Distribution Protocol) should be used for pseudowire signaling in the VSI (Virtual Switch Instance). In Juniper, this is typically configured under `protocols l2vpn` as the default signaling protocol for L2VPN services is LDP. \\n\\nNote: Juniper's L2VPN configuration is more modular and may require additional context (like neighbor settings) for a complete equivalent setup. The above is the direct translation of enabling LDP signaling for L2VPN pseudowires.\", 'trans_template': 'protocols l2vpn'}]]": 1,
