    "['ospf [process-id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0'}]]": 1,
    "['area [area-id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0', 'parent_command': ['set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0'], 'root': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0'}]]": 1,
    "['network [ip-address] [wildcard-mask]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': ['set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0', 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0'], 'root': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI OSPF network command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, we don\\'t use the \"network\" statement like HUAWEI does\\n- Instead, we directly specify which interfaces should participate in OSPF\\n- The Loopback interface (lo0.0 in Juniper) is explicitly added to OSPF area 0.0.0.0\\n- The wildcard mask (0.0.0.0) isn\\'t needed in Juniper as we specify interfaces directly\\n\\nThis achieves the same result as the HUAWEI command, which was advertising the loopback interface\\'s exact IP (1.1.1.1/32) into OSPF area 0.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface lo0.0'}]]": 1,
    "['network [ip-address] [wildcard-mask]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 network 10.1.1.0/24', 'parent_command': ['set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0', 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0'], 'root': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 network 10.1.1.0/24\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 network 10.1.1.0/24'}]]": 1,
    "['cfm md [md-name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 level 5', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 level 5', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 level 5\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Huawei `cfm md md1` command creates a CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) maintenance domain named \"md1\". \\n- In Juniper, the equivalent is configuring an Ethernet CFM maintenance domain under protocols.\\n- I set the default level to 5 (since Huawei doesn\\'t specify in this command, level 5 is commonly used for operator-level domains).\\n- The Juniper command maintains the same domain name \"md1\".', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 level 5'}]]": 1,
    "['ma [ma-name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 level 5'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 level 5', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei \"ma ma1\" command creates a Maintenance Association (MA) under a Maintenance Domain (MD) in CFM (Connectivity Fault Management). In Juniper, the equivalent is configuring an Ethernet CFM maintenance-association under a maintenance-domain.\\n\\nThe Juniper command follows this structure:\\n- `set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management` - Base CFM path\\n- `maintenance-domain md1` - References the MD (md1 in original config)\\n- `maintenance-association ma1` - Creates the MA (ma1 in original config)', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1'}]]": 1,
    "['map vsi [vsi-name]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set forwarding-options cfm-mep maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 l2-vpn-vsi ldp1', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 level 5', 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md1 level 5', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for `map vsi ldp1`:\\n\\n##\\nset forwarding-options cfm-mep maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 l2-vpn-vsi ldp1\\n##\\n\\nThis command associates the CFM maintenance association with the L2VPN VSI (Virtual Switch Instance) named \"ldp1\" in Juniper\\'s syntax, which is functionally equivalent to the Huawei `map vsi ldp1` command that maps the CFM MA to the VSI.', 'trans_template': 'set forwarding-options cfm-mep maintenance-domain md1 maintenance-association ma1 l2-vpn-vsi ldp1'}]]": 1,
